    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter this September 29 slate with a lean, efficient starting five as we navigate the final stretch of the season. Our highest-rated play today is **Sam Antonacci** (58.38), whose top-of-the-order role against Blubaugh provides a significant boost, compounded by a favorable platoon split that pushes his daily efficiency well above his base projection. While **Miguel Vargas** shares the same matchup, his slightly lower score of 50.48 reflects the reality of hitting in the three-hole against a starter who maintains a respectable 4.04 xERA, though his strong xwOBA keeps him firmly in the \"Marginal\" to \"Strong\" transition zone. **Jackson Merrill** also provides a stable floor (53.09) in his matchup against Boyd; while his left-on-left disadvantage against the starter creates some drag, his ability to drive the ball keeps him ahead of the bench options.\n\nThe bench decision process today was straightforward due to a wave of team off-days for our core stars like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who are all unavailable. With **Luis Robert Jr.** sidelined on the IL, the roster depth is being tested. **Drake Baldwin** (47.58) and **Heliot Ramos** (46.77) round out the lineup today; while both hover in the high-40s, they are our most viable options given the current constraints. **Heliot Ramos** benefits from a park factor bump, though the matchup against Tolle carries risk due to the pitcher's decent skill set. We are essentially playing a \"keep-the-lineup-active\" strategy today; with no elite speed threats currently active to chase that scarce SB category, the focus remains on maintaining our offensive output while preserving our remaining game caps for the final push. There are no immediate weather threats, but we remain vigilant regarding any late-scratches given the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several spots.",
